IMPORT prelude

-- Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Regulations 2019 (Cth) -- the rules an injured Commonwealth employee (or a
-- licensee's employee) meets in the Comcare scheme, with the provisions of the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation
-- Act 1988 that the Regulations fill in (s 4 "medical treatment" and "Entity", s 7(8) and (9), s 8(9B) to (9G), ss 61(1A)
-- and 62(6)).
--
-- Based on content from the Federal Register of Legislation: "Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Regulations 2019",
-- Compilation No. 2 (compilation date 1 April 2024, register id F2024C00663), Commonwealth of Australia, licensed under
-- CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Quotations are from the deposited plain-text conversion at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/F2019L00423.txt; the Act's words quoted are from
-- ../../../safety-rehabilitation-and-compensation-act-1988/registers/source-bundle/C2004A03668.txt (Compilation No. 82).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Negatives follow the rulings of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05 (docs/ENCODING-GUIDE.md section 5): JUST FALSE where the
-- text itself says no; NOTHING where it does not answer, each tagged "NOTHING-kind" with the reason.
--
-- Dates are worked as day serials with the builtins DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_YEAR and
-- DATE_MONTH; nothing imports daydate.

§ `Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Regulations 2019`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`day number of` d MEANS DATE_SERIAL d

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the date of day number` n MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL n

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is on or after` a b MEANS (`day number of` a) AT LEAST (`day number of` b)

§§ `s 6 and Schedule 2 -- Entities and their principal officers`

-- Act s 4(1): "Entity means: (a) an Agency ... (b) a Parliamentary Department ... (c) a person, body, organisation or
-- group of persons prescribed for this paragraph." "principal officer, in relation to an Entity, means ... (c) ... the
-- person prescribed as the principal officer." Reg s 6 and Schedule 2 prescribe seven, each with its principal officer.
DECLARE `My employer` IS ONE OF
    `the Australian Federal Police`
    `the Australian Signals Directorate`
    `the Australian Secret Intelligence Service`
    `the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation`
    `the Commonwealth Grants Commission`
    `the High Court of Australia`
    `the Office of Official Secretary to the Governor-General`
    `another employer`

GIVEN e IS A `My employer`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`Schedule 2 -- the principal officer of my employer` e MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `the Australian Federal Police` THEN JUST "the Commissioner of Police"
    WHEN `the Australian Signals Directorate` THEN JUST "the Director-General of the Australian Signals Directorate"
    WHEN `the Australian Secret Intelligence Service` THEN JUST "the Director-General of the Australian Secret Intelligence Service"
    WHEN `the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation` THEN JUST "the Director-General of Security"
    WHEN `the Commonwealth Grants Commission` THEN JUST "the Chairperson"
    WHEN `the High Court of Australia` THEN JUST "the Chief Executive and Principal Registrar"
    WHEN `the Office of Official Secretary to the Governor-General` THEN JUST "the Official Secretary"
    -- NOTHING-kind: points outside the sources; the employer may still be an Entity under paragraph (a) or (b) of the
    -- Act's definition (an Agency or a Parliamentary Department), which the Regulations do not touch.
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN e IS A `My employer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6 -- my employer is a prescribed Entity` e MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `another employer` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind: points outside the sources (Act s 4(1) "Entity" (a), (b)).
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 7 -- forms of medical treatment`

-- Act s 4(1) "medical treatment means: ... (i) any other form of treatment that is prescribed for the purposes of this
-- definition." Reg s 7(1): "therapeutic treatment by, or under the supervision of, any of the following persons who meet
-- the requirements of subsection (2) ... is prescribed: (a) an occupational therapist; (b) an optometrist; (c) a
-- podiatrist; (d) a psychologist; (e) a speech therapist or speech pathologist." s 7(2): such a person "meets the
-- requirements of this subsection if the person is: (a) registered by a national registration authority (within the
-- meaning of section 8 of the Healthcare Identifiers Act 2010); or (b) if there is no such authority--a member of a
-- relevant professional association."
DECLARE `Kind of practitioner` IS ONE OF
    `an occupational therapist`
    `an optometrist`
    `a podiatrist`
    `a psychologist`
    `a speech therapist or speech pathologist`
    `another kind of practitioner`

DECLARE `Treatment facts` HAS
    `practitioner` IS A `Kind of practitioner`
    `therapeutic treatment by or under the supervision of the practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a national registration authority for the profession` IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered by that authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `member of a relevant professional association` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 7(2) "meets the requirements ... if": an "if" condition, so failing it is the text's no.
GIVEN t IS A `Treatment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 7(2) -- the practitioner meets the requirements` t MEANS
    IF t's `there is a national registration authority for the profession`
    THEN t's `registered by that authority`
    ELSE t's `member of a relevant professional association`

GIVEN t IS A `Treatment facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7 -- the treatment is prescribed medical treatment` t MEANS
    CONSIDER t's `practitioner`
    -- NOTHING-kind: scope limit; s 7 prescribes only the five listed professions, and the Act's own paragraphs (a) to
    -- (h) of "medical treatment" may still cover the treatment (a doctor, a physiotherapist, a direction by a doctor).
    WHEN `another kind of practitioner` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        IF NOT (t's `therapeutic treatment by or under the supervision of the practitioner`)
        -- NOTHING-kind: scope limit; s 7 covers therapeutic treatment only (fork F2).
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE IF `s 7(2) -- the practitioner meets the requirements` t
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 8A with Act s 7(8), (9) -- diseases suffered by firefighters`

-- Act s 7(8): "If an employee: (a) suffers a disease mentioned in the following table; and (b) before the disease was
-- sustained, was employed as a firefighter for the qualifying period mentioned for that disease; and (c) was exposed to
-- the hazards of a fire scene during that period; and (d) in the case of a cancer of a kind covered by item 13 of the
-- following table--satisfies the conditions (if any) prescribed for such a cancer; the employment is ... taken to have
-- contributed, to a significant degree, to the contraction of the disease, unless the contrary is established."
-- Items 1-12 are in the Act; item 13 is "A cancer of a kind prescribed for this table", with "The period prescribed for
-- such a cancer". Reg s 8A prescribes eight cancers and their periods, and no conditions (finding 2).
DECLARE `Disease` IS ONE OF
    `primary site brain cancer`
    `primary site bladder cancer`
    `primary site kidney cancer`
    `primary non-Hodgkins lymphoma`
    `primary leukemia`
    `primary site breast cancer`
    `primary site testicular cancer`
    `multiple myeloma`
    `primary site prostate cancer`
    `primary site ureter cancer`
    `primary site colorectal cancer`
    `primary site oesophageal cancer`
    `primary site lung cancer`
    `primary site skin cancer`
    `primary site cervical cancer`
    `primary site ovarian cancer`
    `primary site penile cancer`
    `primary site pancreatic cancer`
    `primary site thyroid cancer`
    `malignant mesothelioma`
    `another disease`

-- Item 13 of the Act's table, filled by reg s 8A items 1-8.
GIVEN d IS A `Disease`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8A -- the disease is a prescribed cancer` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `primary site lung cancer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `primary site skin cancer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `primary site cervical cancer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `primary site ovarian cancer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `primary site penile cancer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `primary site pancreatic cancer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `primary site thyroid cancer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `malignant mesothelioma` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The qualifying period in years: Act s 7(8) items 1-12, reg s 8A items 1-8.
GIVEN d IS A `Disease`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 7(8) -- the qualifying period in years` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `primary site brain cancer` THEN JUST 5
    WHEN `primary site bladder cancer` THEN JUST 15
    WHEN `primary site kidney cancer` THEN JUST 15
    WHEN `primary non-Hodgkins lymphoma` THEN JUST 15
    WHEN `primary leukemia` THEN JUST 5
    WHEN `primary site breast cancer` THEN JUST 10
    WHEN `primary site testicular cancer` THEN JUST 10
    WHEN `multiple myeloma` THEN JUST 15
    WHEN `primary site prostate cancer` THEN JUST 15
    WHEN `primary site ureter cancer` THEN JUST 15
    WHEN `primary site colorectal cancer` THEN JUST 15
    WHEN `primary site oesophageal cancer` THEN JUST 15
    WHEN `primary site lung cancer` THEN JUST 15
    WHEN `primary site skin cancer` THEN JUST 15
    WHEN `primary site cervical cancer` THEN JUST 10
    WHEN `primary site ovarian cancer` THEN JUST 10
    WHEN `primary site penile cancer` THEN JUST 15
    WHEN `primary site pancreatic cancer` THEN JUST 10
    WHEN `primary site thyroid cancer` THEN JUST 10
    WHEN `malignant mesothelioma` THEN JUST 15
    -- NOTHING-kind: the table names no period for a disease it does not list.
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `Firefighter facts` HAS
    `the disease` IS A `Disease`
    `years employed as a firefighter before the disease was sustained` IS A NUMBER
    `the relevant authority is satisfied that firefighting or related duties made up a not insubstantial portion of the duties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed as a firefighter by the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth authority or a licensed corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exposed to the hazards of a fire scene during that period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the disease was sustained` IS A DATE
    `the day of the decision` IS A DATE

-- Reg s 36: s 8A "applies in relation to a decision made under the Act ... after the commencement of that instrument
-- [17 December 2022], in relation to a cancer mentioned in that section sustained by an employee on or after 4 July
-- 2011." A scope limit with no "only".
GIVEN f IS A `Firefighter facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36 -- s 8A applies to the decision` f MEANS
        `is on or after` (f's `the day the disease was sustained`) (DATE_FROM_DMY 4 7 2011)
    AND `is on or after` (f's `the day of the decision`) (DATE_FROM_DMY 17 12 2022)

-- Act s 7(8) and (9) came from the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Amendment (Fair Protection for Firefighters)
-- Act 2011 (No. 182, 2011), which commenced on 7 December 2011 and has its own application provision (Sch. 1 items 2,
-- 3), per endnote 3 of the deposited Act. That application provision is not deposited; reg s 36's 4 July 2011 is taken
-- as its date for the Act's items too (fork F15). A decision before 7 December 2011 was made before s 7(8) was in the
-- Act, under an earlier compilation that is not deposited.
GIVEN f IS A `Firefighter facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Act s 7(8) applies in time` f MEANS
        `is on or after` (f's `the day the disease was sustained`) (DATE_FROM_DMY 4 7 2011)
    AND `is on or after` (f's `the day of the decision`) (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 12 2011)

GIVEN f IS A `Firefighter facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(8) -- my employment is taken to have contributed to the disease` f MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 7(8) -- the qualifying period in years` (f's `the disease`)
    -- (a) fails: the "If" of s 7(8) is not met, and s 7(8) gives no presumption. Sections 7(1) and (2) are untouched
    -- (s 7(10)).
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN JUST period THEN
        -- First the time limit (NOTHING-kind: scope limit, the commencement and application of the 2011 amending Act,
        -- whose application provision is not deposited; fork F15), then reg s 36 for a s 8A cancer (NOTHING-kind: scope
        -- limit, reg s 36 has no "only"; ruling of 2026-11-05 (c); fork F4). s 7(9)(a): the employee "is taken to have
        -- been employed as a firefighter if the relevant authority is satisfied that firefighting or related duties made
        -- up a not insubstantial portion of his or her duties"; that satisfaction is its own input (fork F16).
        IF NOT (`Act s 7(8) applies in time` f)
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE IF (`s 8A -- the disease is a prescribed cancer` (f's `the disease`)) AND (NOT (`s 36 -- s 8A applies to the decision` f))
             THEN NOTHING
             ELSE IF     (f's `years employed as a firefighter before the disease was sustained`) AT LEAST period
                     AND f's `the relevant authority is satisfied that firefighting or related duties made up a not insubstantial portion of the duties`
                     AND f's `employed as a firefighter by the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth authority or a licensed corporation`
                     AND f's `exposed to the hazards of a fire scene during that period`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 8-11 with Act s 8(9B)-(9G) -- indexation of normal weekly earnings`

-- Act s 8(9B): normal weekly earnings "must, if the employee has ceased, or ceases, to be employed by the Commonwealth or
-- a licensed corporation, be further increased, with effect from each indexation date". s 8(9E): they "must, with effect
-- from 1 July in each year, be further increased by the amount under subsection (9F) if, in the 12 months immediately
-- preceding that 1 July: (a) there was no increase in those earnings under subsection (6), (7) or (9); and (b) there was
-- no reduction in those earnings under subsection (9)." Reg ss 8 and 10 prescribe the Wage Price Index for each; reg
-- ss 9 and 11 set the same formula for each.
DECLARE `Which indexation` IS ONE OF
    `s 8(9B) and regulations ss 8 and 9 (after leaving Commonwealth employment)`
    `s 8(9E) and regulations ss 10 and 11 (no other change in 12 months)`
    `both s 8(9B) and s 8(9E) on the words of the Act`
    `neither`

GIVEN `ceased` IS A BOOLEAN, `increased under s 8(6), (7) or (9) in the 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN, `reduced under s 8(9) in the 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Which indexation`
`s 8(9B), (9E) -- the indexation that applies on 1 July` `ceased` `increased under s 8(6), (7) or (9) in the 12 months` `reduced under s 8(9) in the 12 months` MEANS
    IF `ceased` AND `nine E applies`
    THEN `both s 8(9B) and s 8(9E) on the words of the Act`
    ELSE IF `ceased`
         THEN `s 8(9B) and regulations ss 8 and 9 (after leaving Commonwealth employment)`
         ELSE IF `nine E applies`
              THEN `s 8(9E) and regulations ss 10 and 11 (no other change in 12 months)`
              ELSE `neither`
    WHERE
        `nine E applies` MEANS
                (NOT `increased under s 8(6), (7) or (9) in the 12 months`)
            AND (NOT `reduced under s 8(9) in the 12 months`)

-- Act s 8(9C): "the indexation date, in relation to a cessation of employment, is: (a) the 1 July next following: (i)
-- the date on which this Act receives the Royal Assent; or (ii) the date of that cessation of employment; whichever last
-- occurs; and (b) each subsequent 1 July." Only cessations after the Royal Assent (1988) are asked about; "next
-- following" a cessation on 1 July is read as the 1 July a year later (fork F6).
GIVEN c IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 8(9C) -- the first indexation date after I ceased` c MEANS
    IF (DATE_MONTH c) LESS THAN 7
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 (DATE_YEAR c)
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 ((DATE_YEAR c) PLUS 1)

-- Reg ss 9 and 11: "F is the greater of the following: (a) the number (worked out to 4 decimal places and rounded up to
-- 3 decimal places) obtained by dividing the index number by the previous index number; (b) 1.000." "Worked out to 4
-- decimal places" is read as cut off at the fourth place, and "rounded up" as raised to the next 0.001 whenever anything
-- is left at the fourth place (fork F7).
GIVEN `index number` IS A NUMBER, `previous index number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ss 9, 11 -- F` `index number` `previous index number` MEANS
    IF `rounded` GREATER THAN 1
    THEN `rounded`
    ELSE 1
    WHERE
        `to 4 places` MEANS (FLOOR ((`index number` DIVIDED BY `previous index number`) TIMES 10000)) DIVIDED BY 10000
        `rounded` MEANS (CEILING (`to 4 places` TIMES 1000)) DIVIDED BY 1000

-- Reg ss 9 and 11: the further increase "is to be calculated, to 3 decimal places and rounded up to 2 decimal places, in
-- accordance with the following formula". The formula itself is lost from the deposit ("the following formula: where:"
-- with nothing between). Its terms are F and WE ("the normal weekly earnings that applied immediately before the
-- indexation date"), and the note says "there will be a further increase ... only if F is greater than 1.000"; the
-- increase is taken as WE x (F - 1) (finding 1, fork F8).
GIVEN `WE` IS A NUMBER, `index number` IS A NUMBER, `previous index number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ss 9, 11 -- the further increase in dollars` `WE` `index number` `previous index number` MEANS
    (CEILING (`to 3 places` TIMES 100)) DIVIDED BY 100
    WHERE
        `raw increase` MEANS `WE` TIMES ((`ss 9, 11 -- F` `index number` `previous index number`) MINUS 1)
        `to 3 places` MEANS (FLOOR (`raw increase` TIMES 1000)) DIVIDED BY 1000

§§ `s 11A with Act ss 61(1A), 62(6) -- the periods for deciding my claim and my request`

-- Act s 61(1A): "The determining authority must consider and determine each claim for compensation under section 14
-- within the period prescribed by the regulations." Reg s 11A(1): (a) for an injury (other than a disease) or its
-- aggravation, "the period of 20 calendar days"; (b) for a disease, "the period of 60 calendar days"; each "starting on
-- the day the determining authority receives the claim made in accordance with section 54 of the Act and worked out
-- disregarding any calendar day covered by subsection (3)". The day of receipt is the first day.
DECLARE `Kind of claim` IS ONE OF
    `an injury other than a disease, or its aggravation`
    `a disease, or its aggravation`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 11A(1) -- calendar days` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an injury other than a disease, or its aggravation` THEN 20
    WHEN `a disease, or its aggravation` THEN 60

-- Reg s 11A(3): a calendar day is covered "if it is in a period: (a) starting on the day referred to in column 2 of an
-- item ...; and (b) ending on the day referred to in column 3". Items 1-5: a medical examination under Act s 57; a
-- request for information under s 58; a requirement on my employer under s 71; my advice that I will give further
-- evidence; a further medical report the authority considers reasonable and necessary. Each period is entered by its
-- first and last day; both days are covered.
DECLARE `Paused period` HAS
    `first day` IS A DATE
    `last day` IS A DATE

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, ps IS A LIST OF `Paused period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11A(3) -- the day is covered` n ps MEANS
    any (GIVEN p YIELD (n AT LEAST (`day number of` (p's `first day`))) AND (n AT MOST (`day number of` (p's `last day`)))) ps

-- Counts forward from day n, needing `left` more days that count; returns the day number of the last of them.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `left` IS A NUMBER, ps IS A LIST OF `Paused period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last counted day from` n `left` ps MEANS
    IF `s 11A(3) -- the day is covered` n ps
    THEN `the last counted day from` (n PLUS 1) `left` ps
    ELSE IF `left` AT MOST 1
         THEN n
         ELSE `the last counted day from` (n PLUS 1) (`left` MINUS 1) ps

-- Reg s 37(a): s 11A applies to "a claim for compensation under section 14 of the Act made in accordance with section 54
-- of the Act on or after the commencement of that instrument" (1 April 2024). A scope limit.
GIVEN `received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 37 -- s 11A applies` `received` MEANS `is on or after` `received` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2024)

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of claim`, `received` IS A DATE, `made in accordance with s 54` IS A BOOLEAN, ps IS A LIST OF `Paused period`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 11A(1) -- the last day for determining my claim` k `received` `made in accordance with s 54` ps MEANS
    IF (NOT `made in accordance with s 54`) OR (NOT (`s 37 -- s 11A applies` `received`))
    -- NOTHING-kind: scope limit; the period runs only from receipt of a claim made in accordance with s 54, and s 37
    -- applies s 11A only to claims made on or after 1 April 2024 (fork F9).
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the date of day number` (`the last counted day from` (`day number of` `received`) (`s 11A(1) -- calendar days` k) ps))

-- Reg s 11A(2): for Act s 62(6), "the determining authority must decide a request made by a claimant to reconsider a
-- decision within the period of 30 calendar days, starting on the day the determining authority receives the request."
-- No day is disregarded: s 11A(3) is "For the purposes of subsection (1)" only (finding 4). Reg s 37(b) applies s 11A
-- to "a request to reconsider a decision under section 38 or 62 of the Act made by a claimant on or after" 1 April 2024;
-- s 11A(2) itself serves only s 62(6) (finding 5).
DECLARE `Kind of request` IS ONE OF
    `reconsideration of a determination on my claim (Act s 62)`
    `reconsideration of a rehabilitation determination (Act s 38)`

GIVEN r IS A `Kind of request`, `received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 11A(2) -- the last day for deciding my request` r `received` MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    -- NOTHING-kind: silent; s 11A(2) prescribes a period for s 62(6) only, and the Act's s 38 points to none here.
    WHEN `reconsideration of a rehabilitation determination (Act s 38)` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `reconsideration of a determination on my claim (Act s 62)` THEN
        IF `is on or after` `received` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2024)
        THEN JUST (`the date of day number` ((`day number of` `received`) PLUS 29))
        -- NOTHING-kind: scope limit (s 37(b)).
        ELSE NOTHING

-- The duties of ss 61(1A) and 62(6) as regulative rules. The day of receipt is time 0 on a scale of day numbers, and
-- WITHIN counts to the last day inclusive (an act at start + WITHIN fulfils it, checked on stable l4).
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF `the determining authority`

DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `determine my claim`
    `decide my request to reconsider`

GIVEN `days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 61(1A) -- the determining authority must determine my claim` `days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the determining authority`
    MUST `determine my claim`
    WITHIN `days allowed`
    LEST BREACH BY `the determining authority` BECAUSE "the claim was not determined within the period prescribed by regulation 11A(1) (Act s 61(1A))"

GIVEN `days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 62(6) -- the determining authority must decide my request` `days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the determining authority`
    MUST `decide my request to reconsider`
    WITHIN `days allowed`
    LEST BREACH BY `the determining authority` BECAUSE "the request was not decided within the 30 calendar days prescribed by regulation 11A(2) (Act s 62(6))"

-- Runs a duty over one act (or none) at a day number. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE matches FULFILLED but
-- not BREACH, so anything else (a breach, or a duty still open) is FALSE. Takes no DEONTIC input and is not exported.
GIVEN `duty` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`, `step` IS A `Step`, `start` IS A NUMBER, `at` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty is kept by an act at` `duty` `step` `start` `at` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `duty` `start` (LIST (EVENT `the determining authority` `step` `at`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Where it stands` IS ONE OF
    `decided within the period`
    `decided after the period ended`
    `not yet decided, and the period has not ended`
    `not yet decided, and the period has ended`

-- Where it is decided, the trace runs the decision itself. Where it is not, the trace asks whether a decision on the
-- day asked about would still keep the duty: if it would, the period has not ended.
GIVEN `duty` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`, `step` IS A `Step`, `received` IS A DATE, `decided` IS A BOOLEAN, `decision day` IS A DATE, `as at` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Where it stands`
`where the duty stands` `duty` `step` `received` `decided` `decision day` `as at` MEANS
    IF `decided`
    THEN IF `the duty is kept by an act at` `duty` `step` (`day number of` `received`) (`day number of` `decision day`)
         THEN `decided within the period`
         ELSE `decided after the period ended`
    ELSE IF `the duty is kept by an act at` `duty` `step` (`day number of` `received`) (`day number of` `as at`)
         THEN `not yet decided, and the period has not ended`
         ELSE `not yet decided, and the period has ended`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of claim`, `received` IS A DATE, `made in accordance with s 54` IS A BOOLEAN, `decided` IS A BOOLEAN, `decision day` IS A DATE, `as at` IS A DATE, ps IS A LIST OF `Paused period`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Where it stands`
`s 61(1A) -- where the determination of my claim stands` k `received` `made in accordance with s 54` `decided` `decision day` `as at` ps MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 11A(1) -- the last day for determining my claim` k `received` `made in accordance with s 54` ps
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind: no prescribed period applies (see the last day above).
    WHEN JUST `last day` THEN
        JUST (`where the duty stands`
                (`s 61(1A) -- the determining authority must determine my claim` ((`day number of` `last day`) MINUS (`day number of` `received`)))
                `determine my claim` `received` `decided` `decision day` `as at`)

GIVEN r IS A `Kind of request`, `received` IS A DATE, `decided` IS A BOOLEAN, `decision day` IS A DATE, `as at` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Where it stands`
`s 62(6) -- where the decision on my request stands` r `received` `decided` `decision day` `as at` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 11A(2) -- the last day for deciding my request` r `received`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind: no prescribed period applies (see the last day above).
    WHEN JUST `last day` THEN
        JUST (`where the duty stands`
                (`s 62(6) -- the determining authority must decide my request` ((`day number of` `last day`) MINUS (`day number of` `received`)))
                `decide my request to reconsider` `received` `decided` `decision day` `as at`)

§§ `Part 4 Division 2 -- when my employer's licence is suspended or revoked`

-- A licensee (a Commonwealth authority or an eligible corporation licensed under Part VIII of the Act) may accept
-- liability for its employees' compensation, manage their claims, or both. Subdivision A (ss 18-25) says what follows
-- when a licensed authority's licence is suspended or revoked; Subdivision B (ss 26-31) when a licensed corporation's
-- licence is revoked. The note to s 19 says only an authority's licence may be suspended (Directions, not deposited).
DECLARE `Who held the licence` IS ONE OF
    `a Commonwealth authority (licensed authority)`
    `a corporation (licensed corporation)`

DECLARE `What happened to the licence` IS ONE OF
    `suspended`
    `revoked`

DECLARE `Licence facts` HAS
    `holder` IS A `Who held the licence`
    `event` IS A `What happened to the licence`
    `the licence covered accepting liability` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the licence covered managing claims` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my injury occurred before the day of revocation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Comcare has decided to manage my claim or arrange its management` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commission has demanded payment under my employer's guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Who is liable` IS ONE OF
    `my employer, and Comcare may pay it during the suspension`
    `my former employer, and Comcare may pay it`
    `Comcare`
    `my former employer`
    `no one under the Act, which has ceased to apply`

GIVEN l IS A `Licence facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Who is liable`
`ss 19, 21, 27, 28 -- who is liable for my compensation` l MEANS
    CONSIDER l's `holder`
    WHEN `a Commonwealth authority (licensed authority)` THEN
        CONSIDER l's `event`
        -- s 19(2): "(a) that liability is not affected by the suspension ...; and (b) during the period of the licence
        -- suspension, Comcare may discharge a liability".
        WHEN `suspended` THEN
            IF l's `the licence covered accepting liability`
            THEN JUST `my employer, and Comcare may pay it during the suspension`
            ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind: s 19(2) is "If the licence authorises ..."; silent otherwise.
        -- s 21(2)(b), (c): the former authority "remains liable" for injury "occurring before the final licence was
        -- revoked", and Comcare may discharge it. s 21(7): "Comcare is liable ... [for injury] occurring on or after the
        -- date of revocation" (not conditioned on the licence's scope).
        WHEN `revoked` THEN
            IF NOT (l's `my injury occurred before the day of revocation`)
            THEN JUST `Comcare`
            ELSE IF l's `the licence covered accepting liability`
                 THEN JUST `my former employer, and Comcare may pay it`
                 ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind: s 21(2) is "If the final licence ... authorised"; silent otherwise.
    WHEN `a corporation (licensed corporation)` THEN
        CONSIDER l's `event`
        -- NOTHING-kind: scope limit; Subdivision B deals only with revocation, and the note to s 19 says a corporation's
        -- licence cannot be suspended.
        WHEN `suspended` THEN NOTHING
        -- s 27(2)(b): "remains liable ... [for injury] occurring before the final licence was revoked". s 27(2)(a) and
        -- s 28(3): it "ceases to be liable" for later injury, and "the Act ceases to apply to the former licensed
        -- corporation and its employees, except as provided by this Subdivision" (finding 6).
        WHEN `revoked` THEN
            IF NOT (l's `my injury occurred before the day of revocation`)
            THEN JUST `no one under the Act, which has ceased to apply`
            ELSE IF l's `the licence covered accepting liability`
                 THEN JUST `my former employer`
                 ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind: s 27(2) is "If the final licence ... authorised"; silent otherwise.

DECLARE `Who manages my claim` IS ONE OF
    `Comcare, in my employer's name, during the suspension`
    `Comcare`
    `my former employer, as if the licence had not been revoked`
    `Comcare, or a person Comcare arranges`
    `not my former employer, and the Act has ceased to apply`

GIVEN l IS A `Licence facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Who manages my claim`
`ss 19, 21, 27, 30 -- who manages my claim` l MEANS
    IF NOT (l's `the licence covered managing claims`)
    -- NOTHING-kind: each of ss 19(3), 21(3) and 27(3) is "If the licence authorises/authorised ... to manage claims".
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER l's `holder`
         WHEN `a Commonwealth authority (licensed authority)` THEN
             CONSIDER l's `event`
             -- s 19(3)(a)(i), (ii): the authority "must not manage those claims" and "Comcare must manage those claims
             -- in the name of the licensed authority".
             WHEN `suspended` THEN JUST `Comcare, in my employer's name, during the suspension`
             -- s 21(3)(a), (b): the former authority must not manage a claim of its employees "whenever occurring", and
             -- "Comcare must manage" them.
             WHEN `revoked` THEN JUST `Comcare`
         WHEN `a corporation (licensed corporation)` THEN
             CONSIDER l's `event`
             WHEN `suspended` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind: scope limit, as above.
             WHEN `revoked` THEN
                 IF l's `my injury occurred before the day of revocation`
                 -- s 30(8): Comcare may decide to manage relevant claims or arrange for a person to manage them;
                 -- otherwise s 27(3)(a): the former corporation "must manage a claim ... as if the final licence had not
                 -- been revoked".
                 THEN IF l's `Comcare has decided to manage my claim or arrange its management`
                      THEN JUST `Comcare, or a person Comcare arranges`
                      ELSE JUST `my former employer, as if the licence had not been revoked`
                 -- s 27(3)(b): it "must not manage a claim ... in respect of any injury ... occurring on or after the day
                 -- of revocation"; s 28(3).
                 ELSE JUST `not my former employer, and the Act has ceased to apply`

-- ss 19(3)(a)(iii), 21(3)(c)(i), 30(11)(a): on receiving a claim, notice or other communication, or being served with
-- proceedings, the (former) licensee must give it to Comcare. No period is set ("on receiving").
GIVEN l IS A `Licence facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 19, 21, 30 -- my employer must pass my claim to Comcare` l MEANS
    IF NOT (l's `the licence covered managing claims`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind: each duty sits under "If the licence authorises ... to manage claims".
    ELSE CONSIDER l's `holder`
         WHEN `a Commonwealth authority (licensed authority)` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a corporation (licensed corporation)` THEN
             CONSIDER l's `event`
             WHEN `suspended` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind: scope limit, as above.
             WHEN `revoked` THEN
                 -- s 30 "applies if the Commission makes a demand for payment under a guarantee"; s 30(11) is about
                 -- "relevant claims", those under s 27(3)(a) (injury before revocation).
                 IF     l's `the Commission has demanded payment under my employer's guarantee`
                    AND l's `my injury occurred before the day of revocation`
                 THEN JUST TRUE
                 ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind: scope limit of s 30 (fork F11).

-- ss 22(1)(d), 28(1)(d): during the preservation period, "unless Comcare arranges for another person to act as the
-- rehabilitation authority for the [employer's] employees in accordance with section 25 [31]--the principal officer of
-- the former licensed [authority/corporation] is taken to be the rehabilitation authority".
DECLARE `My rehabilitation authority` IS ONE OF
    `the principal officer of my former employer`
    `the person Comcare has arranged`

GIVEN `in the preservation period` IS A BOOLEAN, `Comcare has arranged another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `My rehabilitation authority`
`ss 22, 28 -- my rehabilitation authority after revocation` `in the preservation period` `Comcare has arranged another person` MEANS
    IF `Comcare has arranged another person`
    THEN JUST `the person Comcare has arranged`
    ELSE IF `in the preservation period`
         THEN JUST `the principal officer of my former employer`
         -- NOTHING-kind: silent; ss 22 and 28 speak only of the preservation period.
         ELSE NOTHING
